name:           pgqueuer-hs
version:        0.1.0.0
synopsis:       High-performance PostgreSQL background job queue with cron and workflows
description:    A high-throughput, type-safe PostgreSQL-backed job queue for Haskell applications.
                Inspired by pgqueuer in Python, pgqueuer-hs leverages PostgreSQL's LISTEN / NOTIFY
                and `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` for reliable, non-contending, at-least-once distributed job processing.
                .
                Key features:
                * Zero-polling real-time dispatch via PostgreSQL LISTEN / NOTIFY
                * Non-contending job claims using `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED`
                * Dual backend support: `SimpleDb` (postgresql-simple) and `HasqlDb` (binary protocol via Hasql)
                * Declarative Workflow DAG orchestration (`JobTree` and `<~~` operator)
                * Native recurring cron job scheduling
                * Pluggable retry backoff policies (constant, linear, exponential) with full and equal jitter
                * Write batching and rate limiting via `TimedOverflowBuffer` to protect PostgreSQL WAL
                * Full end-to-end distributed tracing support
                .
                For getting started and runnable examples, please see the README on GitHub at
                <https://github.com/tusharad/pgqueuer-hs#readme>.
category:       Database, Concurrency, Distributed Computing
stability:      experimental
homepage:       https://github.com/tusharad/pgqueuer-hs#readme
bug-reports:    https://github.com/tusharad/pgqueuer-hs/issues
author:         Tushar Adhatrao
